  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Built against Akka.NET 1.6.0-beta4.\n\n**New Features**\n\n- SQL Server storage can now use a connection factory instead of a connection string. Pass a `Func<CancellationToken, ValueTask<DbConnection>>` to the new `WithSqlServerStorage(connectionFactory, ...)` overload, or set `SqlServerReminderStorageSettings.ConnectionFactory`, to supply connections yourself, for example with an Azure AD access token in `SqlConnection.AccessToken`. The factory is called once per storage operation, so tokens stay fresh, and the storage still opens and disposes each connection. Set exactly one of `ConnectionString` or `ConnectionFactory`. Existing connection-string overloads are unchanged ([#172](https://github.com/Aaronontheweb/akka-reminders/issues/172), [#173](https://github.com/Aaronontheweb/akka-reminders/pull/173)).\n- Added `ReminderSettings.DefaultMaxDeliveryWindow`, first released in 1.5.73.3. Reminders scheduled without their own `maxDeliveryWindow` get a deadline of `due + DefaultMaxDeliveryWindow`, so overdue reminders expire instead of replaying after a restart or outage. The default remains null (no deadline), and a per-call `maxDeliveryWindow` still wins ([#165](https://github.com/Aaronontheweb/akka-reminders/pull/165), [#166](https://github.com/Aaronontheweb/akka-reminders/pull/166)).\n\n**Dependency Updates**\n\n- Moved to Akka.NET 1.6.0-beta4 (Akka.Cluster.Hosting 1.6.0-beta4). Akka.Serialization.V2 1.6.0-beta4 depends on MessagePack 3.1.12, which fixes [GHSA-qhrr-8q5h-9q3h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qhrr-8q5h-9q3h) in 3.1.8 ([#174](https://github.com/Aaronontheweb/akka-reminders/pull/174)).\n- Pinned `System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs` to 9.0.21. `Microsoft.Data.SqlClient` 6.1.4 brought in 9.0.11, which has [GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7) (moderate) and [GHSA-846f-f764-76mx](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-846f-f764-76mx) (high) ([#174](https://github.com/Aaronontheweb/akka-reminders/pull/174)).",
